config BR2_PACKAGE_WIREGUARD_TOOLS_OPENIPC
	bool "wireguard-tools-openipc"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_WIREGUARD_TOOLS # both install /usr/bin/wg
	help
	  The wg tool for configuring WireGuard tunnels.

	  Buildroot's wireguard-tools requires kernel headers >= 3.10, the
	  oldest kernel the out-of-tree module supports. That rules out
	  toolchains built for a 3.0 vendor kernel even when the board runs
	  a modern kernel with WireGuard in-tree (the neo variants). wg only
	  talks generic netlink to the running kernel and builds against 3.0
	  headers with the NLM_F_DUMP_INTR fallback patch.

	  https://git.zx2c4.com/wireguard-tools
